---
export const prerender = false;
import ProLegalDocument from '../components/ProLegalDocument.astro';
---

<ProLegalDocument
  title="Privacy Policy"
  eyebrow="Your workspace data, explained"
  description="How ImageToURL Pro handles accounts, uploaded images, workspace usage, and subscription data."
  intro="This policy explains what ImageToURL Pro collects, how it is used, who processes it, and the choices available to you."
>
  <section>
    <h2>1. Operator and contact</h2>
    <p>
      ImageToURL Pro is operated by <strong>Bipul Kumar</strong> in India (“ImageToURL”, “we”, “us”, or
      “our”). Contact <a href="mailto:blog.boopul@gmail.com">blog.boopul@gmail.com</a> for privacy questions
      or data requests.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>2. Information we collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Your Google account name, email, avatar, and account identifier when you sign in.</li>
      <li>Images, filenames, folders, visibility choices, and source URLs you upload or import.</li>
      <li>Storage, uploads, delivery, feature usage, request, device, IP, security, and error information.</li>
      <li>Pro promotion, pricing, plan-selection, sign-in, paywall, checkout-start, and feature-interaction events, with a random session identifier, page, CTA location, plan choice, referring hostname, and campaign tags.</li>
      <li>Google Analytics page, campaign, device, and Pro funnel events, including checkout and purchase totals without card details or your email address.</li>
      <li>Customer, subscription, transaction, price, renewal, and cancellation status received from Paddle.</li>
      <li>Information you provide in support, refund, privacy, or abuse communications.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Paddle processes payment credentials. ImageToURL does not receive or store your full card number.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>3. How we use information</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Authenticate your account and operate your workspace.</li>
      <li>Store, organize, secure, and deliver images according to your settings.</li>
      <li>Measure plan usage, prevent abuse, and investigate security problems.</li>
      <li>Activate subscriptions and provide billing, refund, and account support.</li>
      <li>Send essential service, billing, security, and policy communications.</li>
      <li>Improve product reliability and understand aggregate feature usage.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do not sell your personal information or place advertising in the Pro workspace.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>4. Public, unlisted, and private assets</h2>
    <p>
      Public and unlisted asset URLs can be opened by anyone who obtains the URL. Unlisted links are not a
      substitute for access control. Private assets require access through your authenticated owner
      workspace. Do not upload regulated or highly sensitive material unless the service and selected
      visibility are appropriate for that data.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>5. Service providers</h2>
    <p>
      We use <strong>Cloudflare</strong> for application hosting, databases, object storage, network
      delivery, and security; <strong>Google</strong> for account authentication and Google Analytics; and
      <strong>Paddle</strong> as Merchant of Record for checkout, billing, tax handling, fraud prevention,
      receipts, invoices, and buyer support.
    </p>
    <p>
      Information may be processed in countries other than your own through these global providers,
      subject to their safeguards and applicable data-transfer mechanisms.
    </p>
    <p>
      Google Analytics may use cookies or similar identifiers. You can control these through your browser
      settings. We send an internal account identifier for signed-in Pro users, never an email address, so
      journeys between pricing and the workspace can be measured without adding contact data to analytics
      events.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>6. Retention, deletion, and security</h2>
    <p>
      Pro assets are retained while your workspace is active, until you delete them, or until removal is
      required for abuse, security, legal, or operational reasons. Account, support, security, and billing
      records are retained as reasonably necessary for the service and legal obligations.
    </p>
    <p>
      First-party Pro interest events are retained for up to 180 days. These event rows do not store your
      IP address, email address, full referring URL, or payment-card data. When you are signed in, an event
      may be associated with your internal ImageToURL account identifier so subscription steps can be
      measured accurately.
    </p>
    <p>
      Deleted assets may remain briefly in caches or backups. We use HTTPS, access controls, and scoped
      Cloudflare resources, but no online system is perfectly secure. Keep independent backups of
      important files.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>7. Your rights and choices</h2>
    <p>
      Depending on your location, you may request access, correction, deletion, restriction, objection, or
      a portable copy of personal data. Email
      <a href="mailto:blog.boopul@gmail.com?subject=ImageToURL%20privacy%20request">blog.boopul@gmail.com</a>
      from your account email. We may verify identity before completing a request.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>8. Children and changes</h2>
    <p>
      ImageToURL Pro is not directed to children under 13. Users must meet the age required to consent to
      data processing and subscriptions where they live, or have appropriate guardian authorization.
    </p>
    <p>Material policy changes will be posted here and communicated where appropriate.</p>
  </section>
</ProLegalDocument>
